  "bio": "Environmental management tries to identify the factors that have a stake in the conflicts that may rise between meeting the needs but protecting the environment.Environmental challenges… 128 CH — Univ. Req. 14 · Univ. Elec. 8 · Colg. Req. 16 · Spec. Req. 78 · Spec. Elec. 6 · Free Elec. 6. Semester order is a suggested prerequisite-valid sequence — no official one was published. Courses, hours and prerequisites are as published. Note: 5 prerequisite pairs point at each other in the source; they are treated as co-requisites.",
  "bioAr": null,
  "overview": "Environmental management tries to identify the factors that have a stake in the conflicts that may rise between meeting the needs but protecting the environment.Environmental challenges require complex solutions, bringing together scientific, social, political and economic perspectives. This Program will provide students with the interdisciplinary perspective and diverse skillset to help solve environmental problems in a leadership role. Graduates can help the Palestinian community manage environmental concerns responsibly, making a positive impact and supporting the common good.This degree with a specialization in waste management provides students with the skills needed to manage, organize, and respond to issues related to waste production and reduction. By focusing on sustainability and paths forward to address waste produced on a local, national, and international scale, this program provides students with the practical tools and policy-based information necessary to pursue waste management jobs in administrative, scientific, or engineering fields.Environmental management tries to identify the factors that have a stake in the conflicts that may rise between meeting the needs but protecting the environment.Environmental challenges require complex solutions, bringing together scientific, social, political and economic perspectives. This Program will provide students with the interdisciplinary perspective and diverse skillset to help solve environmental problems in a leadership role. Graduates can help the Palestinian community manage environmental concerns responsibly, making a positive impact and supporting the common good.This degree with a specialization in waste management provides students with the skills needed to manage, organize, and respond to issues related to waste production and reduction. By focusing on sustainability and paths forward to address waste produced on a local, national, and international scale, this program provides students with the practical tools and policy-based information necessary to pursue waste management jobs in administrative, scientific, or engineering fields.",
